  "summary": "OpenChamber uses OpenCode to run coding agents, calling official OpenCode APIs through @opencode-ai/sdk/v2; the CLI/Web and VS Code surfaces use the user's installed OpenCode CLI. The CLI exposes commands such as status, connect-url --qr, tunnel start, startup enable, logs, stop, and update, and binds to localhost by default with --lan and --ui-password options. Evidence coverage: 145 of 178 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
